# size 20x5
# A character cut in half, and what must happen to whatever follows it.
#
# Row 1: two bytes of a three-byte character, then an escape sequence. The sequence must still be
#        obeyed - this is the bug that made vim's colour changes print as text across the screen,
#        found by running vim through gozellij and diffing against the same vim in tmux.
# Row 3: a stray continuation byte with no lead byte in front of it.
# Row 5: a lead byte that promises four bytes and gets one, then ordinary text. The text must not
#        be swallowed waiting for bytes that are never coming.
\e[H\xe6\x97\e[34mAFTER-ESCAPE
\e[3;1H\x9ctail
\e[5;1H\xf0OK-ANYWAY
